From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Nguyen <tungnh@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 01:49:48 -0700
Subject: Treat empty intersection target rects as not visible

Remove the !latest_observation->GetGeometry().TargetRect().IsEmpty()
condition in HTMLCapabilityElementBase::OnIntersectionChanged(). When
an ancestor has a singular transform (such as scaleX(0), scaleY(0),
scale(0), or rotateY(90deg)), IntersectionGeometry maps the element's
border box to an empty target rect and reports isVisible() == false
with intersectionRatio() == 1.0. Treating empty target rects as visible
allowed zero-pixel capability elements to remain valid and activatable
via keyboard or accesskey.

Also set a non-zero default font size in capability and geolocation
unit test fixtures so elements do not collapse to zero height in tests.

